{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790987719,"nonce":"cDieCkn2KUczH2T7e3dnVs21VKw=","title":"Focus and disabled: state for focus:, disabled: and keyboard","message":"tw refuses focus:, focus-visible:, focus-within:, disabled:, group-hover: and peer-hover: because ashui has no focus model and no disabled state. Needed: a focused element per window (Tab order from the tree, focus on press of a focusable element), keyboard events routed to it (hlwindow KeyboardInput), a disabled flag per element that also stops Pointer from pressing it, and group/peer relations (an element reading an ancestor's or sibling's Interaction). Then the variants compose exactly as hover:/active: do in Tw. Text input (e532fc0) needs the same focus model.","files":null}]}